                        "review": "There are AAA games developed by large teams, and then there are games made by small groups or even individuals. This one is a small gem developed by a single dev.\n\nSetting the scene, I played [i]Gorillas[/i] on MS-DOS as a child with friends, throwing bananas at each other. We had a blast - literally. I’m a simple man, and it takes very little to make me happy. I love playing all the polished AAA stuff, but this kind of game holds a special place in my heart. You can truly feel the dev’s dedication.\n\nI think artillery games are pretty fun in general for a quick round, and even more so if you’re not playing alone (which might turn into a longer session). When you add all the crazy weapons the dev included, the old-school but neatly done graphics, and some beers (or Diet Coke, fwiw), the mayhem can begin. That’s what I love about it.\n\nOne more thing: I was positively surprised that a bug I reported regarding playing the game on Steam Deck was fixed just a couple of days later. I would never have expected that!\n\nSo my final assessment is: The €7 I pay in Germany are worth it. If you don’t like retro graphics reminding you of the past, if you don’t like artillery games, or if you don’t like ridiculous weapons and handcrafted art, leave this game be. Otherwise: Shoot away!",
